    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1032">

                <pb facs="0777" n="661" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg661"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 123B641/18.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul General Hanna to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate General</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Monterey</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I earnestly recommend the diplomatic representatives at Vera Cruz of friendly
                    nations be requested to take action and prompt measures to bring about the
                    release from prison of Vice Consul Silliman at Saltillo, also Consul Bonney at
                    San Luis Potosi, and take them and their American colonies out of the Federal
                    territory. Both Consuls are understood to still be in prison; also several
                    American citizens.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
